      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b0",
      "text": "4.1 Concept Lifecycle\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        74.42,
        189.48,
        85.33
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        297,
        757,
        341
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.91,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Bold",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 21,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b1",
      "text": "By tracking the residual stream across model depth, concept formation is empirically distinguishable\nas a sequence of allocation regions rather than a single allocation followed by decay.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        94.83,
        540.19,
        119.28
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        379,
        2160,
        477
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.8,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 187,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b2",
      "text": "Early layers (Context and Syntax)\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        128.89,
        261.4,
        139.8
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        515,
        1045,
        559
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.91,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Bold",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 33,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b3",
      "text": "In early layers, the residual stream primarily resolves local context, grammar, and surface token\nrelationships. Projecting contrastive datasets into this space generally produces heavily entangled\nactivations; the separation metric is near zero \u2014 the contrastive classes are not yet linearly\ndistinguishable at these depths.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        149.02,
        540.58,
        200.58
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        596,
        2162,
        802
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.02,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 325,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b4",
      "text": "However, the scored detector applied to this paper\u2019s own corpus does find CAZes at the earliest\nstored layers (0\u20131) in tens of concept \u00d7 model pairs, concentrated in concepts with strong lexical\ncues. Credibility is the clearest case: using an independent method (surface lexical cues, not the\nscored detector), the validation paper separately resolves credibility below 25% depth in 9 of 28\nmodels ([Henry, 2026c] \u00a73.3). Layer-indexing convention. Extraction excludes the model\u2019s\npre-transformer embedding output (HuggingFace hidden_states[0]): stored layer 0 is the first\ntransformer block\u2019s output, stored layer l is the output of block l+1, and depth percentages are\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.16,
        209.99,
        540.49,
        302.44
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        284,
        839,
        2161,
        1209
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.02,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Regular",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 670,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b5",
      "text": "taken over the N block outputs. These earliest-layer CAZes therefore sit at the first one or two\ntransformer blocks, not at the raw embedding. Most are gentle-to-moderate (score < 0.1) and\nplausibly reflect near-lexical structure already present in early layers \u2014 concept-associated tokens\ncarrying distinctive early-block geometry, a property of the tokenizer and training corpus rather\nthan deep computation; direct token-embedding alignment does not confirm this account (\u00a75.6).\nWe term these embedding CAZes \u2014 a label for their near-lexical, earliest-layer character, not\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.44,
        304.84,
        542.33,
        383.73
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        285,
        1219,
        2169,
        1534
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.02,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 575,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b6",
      "text": "a claim that they occur before any transformer processing (the literal embedding layer is not in\nthe extracted tensor) \u2014 to distinguish them from active CAZes where the model\u2019s attention and\nMLP computations allocate geometry to serve a concept. Practitioners using CAZ profiles should\nbe aware that embedding CAZes may not respond to the same interventions as active CAZes.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        386.13,
        540.21,
        437.69
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        1544,
        2160,
        1750
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.02,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 374,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b7",
      "text": "CAZ Chain (Concept Allocation)\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        447.29,
        254.91,
        458.2
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        1789,
        1019,
        1832
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.91,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Bold",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 30,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b8",
      "text": "As the residual stream deepens, geometric directions are allocated to concepts in contiguous depth\nregions \u2014 the CAZes. A persistent direction in activation space may serve one concept at shallow\nlayers, be reallocated to a different concept at a mid-depth CAZ, and reallocated again at a deeper\none. For a given concept, the separation metric S(l) reflects when that concept holds a strong claim\non one or more geometric directions; a single concept typically participates in multiple CAZes across\ndepth (mean 2.20 per concept per model under scored detection), ranging from major CAZes (score\n> 0.5) to gentle allocation regions (score < 0.05; Terminology).\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.15,
        467.43,
        540.57,
        559.63
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        284,
        1869,
        2162,
        2238
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.87,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 659,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b9",
      "text": "Late layers (Logit Projection)\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        569.24,
        235.52,
        580.14
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        2276,
        942,
        2320
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.91,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Bold",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 30,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24856_p10_b10",
      "text": "In the final layers, the model transitions from abstract representation to concrete next-token\nprediction. The residual stream is projected toward the unembedding matrix. Concept geometry\nmay degrade or re-entangle as abstract directions give way to vocabulary-specific structure. This is\nthe only phase where separation genuinely decays; earlier apparent \u201cdecay\u201d between CAZ peaks\nmay instead reflect reallocation of the direction to a different concept.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        589.37,
        540.61,
        654.48
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        2357,
        2162,
        2617
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.02,
      "font_name": "LMRoman10-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 455,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
